PS- 1910. Remove All Occurrences of a Substring
Given two strings s and part, perform the following operation on s until all occurrences of the substring part are removed:
Find the leftmost occurrence of the substring part and remove it from s.
Return s after removing all occurrences of part.

Example: Input: s = "daabcbaabcbc", part = "abc"
Output: "dab"

/* CODE */
/* KMP */

/* STACK O(mn), O(n) */
class Solution {
    public String removeOccurrences(String s, String part) {
        Stack<Character> stack = new Stack<>();
        for(char c : s.toCharArray()) {
            stack.push(c);
            if(stack.size() >= part.length() && stack.peek() == part.charAt(part.length()-1)){  //check part is in s or not
                StringBuilder temp = new StringBuilder();
                for(int i = 0; i < part.length(); i++){
                    temp.append(stack.pop());
                }
                temp.reverse();
                if(!temp.toString().equals(part)){  //if part is not equal to s put them back in stack
                    for(char ch : temp.toString().toCharArray()) {
                        stack.push(ch);
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        StringBuilder ans = new StringBuilder();
        while(!stack.isEmpty()) {
            ans.append(stack.pop());
        }
        return ans.reverse().toString();
    }
}


/*
LOGIC---
Why Stack?
When you remove p string. you also need to again see the previous char in s. Menaing access something previous on top. => stack makes this efficient

APPROACH---
Check whether p string occurs in s when s is in stack by comapring last character is on top of stack.
It means that if you've got [xyabc] in the stack then only remove c , b, a from the stack and then continue processing the string

ALGORITHM---
Push character of s in stack.
stack.length>=p.length && stac.peek()==p.charAt(n-1) => take out elements from stack and check whether equal to part

if equal move forward
otherwise push back in stack

Once iterated through string -> output it (reversse the stack)

*/


/* BRUTE FORCE */
class Solution {
    public String removeOccurrences(String s, String part){
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder(s);
        while(sb.indexOf(part)!=-1){
            int occurenceindex = sb.indexOf(part);
            sb.delete(occurenceindex, occurenceindex+part.length());
        }
    return sb.toString();
    }
}

